() Tj
T*
(3. Backend Runtime Entry Point) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The backend uses `backend/app.py` as the Vercel entry point.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Important detail:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Vercel imports `app.py` directly by file path.) Tj
T*
(- Because of that, `backend/app.py` adds the `backend` directory to `sys.path` before) Tj
T*
(  importing `src.main`.) Tj
T*
(- This avoids `ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'src'`.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(4. Database Migrations on Vercel) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The working approach was:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- run `alembic upgrade head` during the build) Tj
T*
(- let the app start after migrations finish successfully) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(This ensures the production database schema is up to date for the deployed backend) Tj
T*
(version.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(5. Mail Template Directory Fix) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Vercel deploys the app under a read-only filesystem location.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(That caused this runtime problem before:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- `OSError: [Errno 30] Read-only file system: '/var/task/src/templates'`) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The fix that worked:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- keep `backend/src/templates/.gitkeep` so the templates folder is bundled) Tj
T*
(- update `backend/src/mail.py` so it uses the bundled templates folder if it exists) Tj
T*
(- otherwise fall back to a writable temp directory instead of trying to create folders in) Tj
T*
(  the deployed source tree) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(6. Trusted Host Fix) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The backend also needed host normalization for Vercel domains.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The working fix in `backend/src/middleware.py`:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- allow `localhost`) Tj
T*
(- allow `127.0.0.1`) Tj
T*
(- allow `*.vercel.app`) Tj
T*
(- allow the hosts extracted from configured frontend and backend URLs) Tj
T*
(- allow the host from `VERCEL_URL`) Tj
ET
