(- the backend is also running locally on your machine) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(It does not work from a deployed Vercel site because `localhost` would then mean the) Tj
T*
(visitor's browser machine, not the deployed backend.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(4. Frontend Runtime API Fix) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The frontend now normalizes `VITE_API_BASE_URL` before using it.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(This protects against three cases:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- local development value like `http://localhost:8000`) Tj
T*
(- production value like `https://one-gms-api.vercel.app`) Tj
T*
(- mistakenly pasted dashboard value like `VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://one-gms-) Tj
T*
(  api.vercel.app`) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(This normalization is used in:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- `frontend/src/api/http.js`) Tj
T*
(- `frontend/vite.config.js`) Tj
T*
(- `frontend/apiBaseUrl.js`) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(5. Redeploy Requirement) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Vite environment variables are compiled into the frontend bundle at build time.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(That means:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- changing a Vercel frontend environment variable does not change the currently deployed) Tj
T*
(  JavaScript) Tj
T*
(- the frontend must be rebuilt and redeployed after the env var changes) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(If the Vercel UI refuses to redeploy a canceled deployment, use a fresh commit.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Safe empty commit example:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(    git commit --allow-empty -m "Trigger frontend rebuild with updated API base URL") Tj
T*
(    git push origin main) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(6. Frontend Verification) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(After the correct frontend deployment goes live:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- login requests should go to `https://one-gms-api.vercel.app/api/v1/auth/login`) Tj
T*
(- they should not go to `http://localhost:8000/api/v1/auth/login`) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(If the browser console shows:) Tj
T*
() Tj
ET
